# These files are read by DSH as UTF-8 and are full of Russian text. An encoding
# or line-ending round trip through a CP1251-aware tool is what corrupted them
# once already, so the repository pins both properties explicitly.
#
# -text stops git from touching line endings. Every skill file is already LF and
# must stay byte-identical to what DSH reads.
# working-tree-encoding is deliberately NOT set: the files are plain UTF-8, and
# asking git to transcode them would reintroduce the risk.
* -text

# Skill documents are UTF-8 with no BOM and LF endings.
*.md -text
*.yaml -text
*.yml -text

# Binary or generated content, never diffed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
